# Force LF on files that run inside the Linux container, regardless of the host's
# core.autocrlf setting. CRLF here would break `bash` and the Docker build.
# Never line-ending-convert a binary. core.autocrlf=true is on for this checkout, and a
# PDF or PNG that gets CRs inserted on clone is silently corrupt: it commits fine on the
# machine that made it and fails to open on the machine that cloned it. That is exactly
# the path the dataset takes to a teammate.
*.pdf           binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.webp          binary
*.npz           binary
*.db            binary
*.docx          binary
*.pptx          binary

*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
docker/**       text eol=lf
